<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's public debt up $1.15 bln in Q1.</title>
<headline>Argentina's public debt up $1.15 bln in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's public debt rose by $1.15 billion in the first quarter ended March 31 to $98.26 billion, the Economy Ministry said Friday.</p>
<p>It said the government issued debt for a total $2.43 billion during the period.</p>
<p>But a rise of the dollar -- to which the peso is pegged at par by law -- compared with European currencies and the yen sliced off $1.7 billion.  </p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0652))</p>
